---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Bianca Ragsdale: senior technical writer, documentation manager, and docs-as-code advocate.">
  <PageHeader title="About" />

  <div class="prose prose-zinc max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
    {/* TODO: write this in your own voice. Drafted from the resume as a starting point. */}
    <p>
      I am a senior technical writer with more than a decade in documentation, from managing a docs team at RED Digital Cinema to serving as the sole technical writer at LandingAI, where I own documentation strategy and execution for an AI product.
    </p>
    <p>
      Lately my work sits at the intersection of writing and tooling: migrating docs to docs-as-code platforms, turning raw OpenAPI specs into publishable API references, and building agentic workflows that keep documentation in sync with the code it describes.
    </p>
    <p>
      I studied English at UC Irvine, with minors in Spanish and Management. I am based in Los Angeles, California.
    </p>

    <h2>Résumé</h2>
    {/* not-prose: keeps Typography's link styles from recoloring the buttons. */}
    <p class="not-prose flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/BiancaRagsdale-Resume.pdf" class="btn-secondary">Download résumé (PDF)</a>
      <a href="/BiancaRagsdale-Resume.md" class="btn-secondary">Markdown version</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Outside of Work</h2>
    <p>When I am not creating documentation, I like to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Hike, especially in Griffith Park.</li>
      <li>Solve crossword puzzles.</li>
      <li>Read. Right now I am exploring books about Hawaii and the history of AI.</li>
      <li>Go to live concerts. Some of my favorite venues are the Troubadour, the Hollywood Bowl, and the Greek Theatre.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
